        },
        {
          v: "4.1.0",
          d: "Sep 17, 2026",
          t: "Major broadcasting infrastructure upgrade across the ABF Network. Deployed a second streaming server with automated DNS failover and recovery, powered by health checks every minute. Added 16 emergency audio streams across both servers for Radio ABF and ABF 2, covering MP3 HD, MP3 SD, AAC and FLAC. Automated weekly recording, validation, synchronization and backup retention ensure that emergency audio remains up to date. Our customized Icecast-KH version also introduces a source-code fix for public stream URLs behind HTTPS reverse proxies, improving Xiph directory registration. Automatic failover and recovery have been successfully tested, strengthening broadcasting continuity and reliability across both stations."
        },
		    {
			v: "4.0.0",
			d: "Sep 14, 2026",
			t: "Major ABF Network expansion. ABF 2 — The Hits Frequency officially joins RadioABF as a second fully integrated station, with its own live streams, Now Playing, music history, community voting, charts, news and dedicated visual identity. Cross-station navigation and network-wide news have been introduced, alongside shared music metadata and automated artwork enrichment. Streaming, Directus integration and deployment infrastructure have also been refined for a more reliable multi-station platform."
			},
			{
          v: "3.5.5",
          d: "Mar 24, 2026",
          t: "Improved artwork consistency across RadioABF. Fixed mismatched covers between Now Playing, Votes, Homepage and Insights. Artwork delivery is now more reliable and optimized, ensuring consistent visuals across all sections. Background processing and asset handling have been enhanced for better stability. API refresh logic has also been optimized for smoother updates and improved realtime performance."
          },
		  {
          v: "3.5.4",
          d: "Mar 15, 2026",
          t: "New Podcasts experience added to RadioABF. This release introduces a dedicated Podcasts page for ABF Club replays, powered by automatic schedule matching and archive retrieval from the latest 7 days of antenna recordings. Podcast sessions now open directly in the global RadioABF player with a dedicated replay mode, while direct source exposure has been removed from the interface. Desktop and mobile navigation were updated to integrate the new Podcasts section across the site."
          },
          {
            v: "3.5.3",
            d: "Mar 13, 2026",
            t: "This update introduces the new Studio Monitoring page, a real-time audio analysis environment integrated directly with the RadioABF player. It provides live VU meters, waveform monitoring, stereo field visualization, spectrum analysis, frequency band energy tracking and advanced signal metrics such as crest factor, stereo width and spectral centroid. The interface follows the RadioABF design system and offers a premium studio-style monitoring experience directly from the web player."
          },
          {
            v: "3.5.2",
            d: "Mar 10, 2026",
            t: "This update introduces a new Airplay Insights subpage integrated into the Music Portal, separating listener features from automatic rotation analytics while keeping a consistent interface. The Insights page includes a live Now Playing block, expanded Most Played, Trending Now and Most Played Today charts, and a larger New Entries panel. Airplay counting logic was also refined to eliminate duplicate spins and improve realtime chart accuracy."
          },
          {
            v: "3.5.1",
            d: "Mar 09, 2026",
            t: "Music Portal refinements and stability improvements. This update introduces a smarter track lifecycle system powered by Directus, allowing RadioABF to track the first time a track enters rotation and display accurate NEW badges across Now Playing, Last Played and New Entries sections. Live show identifiers such as ABF CLUB are now excluded from the new-track logic to avoid false positives. Cover artwork reliability was improved with better fallback handling and smarter caching behavior, ensuring covers remain stable across page navigation and auto-refresh."
          },
          {
            v: "3.5.0",
            d: "Mar 05, 2026",
            t: "Major infrastructure update. RadioABF now operates on a dedicated three-server architecture: abf-front hosts the main website radioabf.com, abf-cms runs the content management and monitoring environment, and abf-stream serves as the public streaming edge delivering listener traffic via HTTPS relay and HLS proxy at stream.radioabf.com. Audio automation and encoding continue to run through a private provider source. Streaming endpoints were simplified with a universal HLS master playlist and a low-bandwidth fallback, improving compatibility across Safari, mobile devices and external players."
          },
          {
            v: "3.4.2",
            d: "Mar 02, 2026",
